# ansible/.ansible-lint-ignore — BASELINE of pre-existing ansible-lint violations (moderate profile).
# Generated 2026-10-01 when ansible-lint became a CI gate (docs/procedures/ci.md).
# Each line is "<path> <rule>" and mutes that rule for that whole file (reported as a warning).
# So: a NEW file, or a NEW rule in a listed file, fails CI; another violation of a rule that is
# already listed for the same file is NOT caught — fix files and delete their lines to tighten.
# Never add lines to make a new change pass — fix the change.
# Tracked in docs/operations/open-questions.md ("ansible-lint baseline").
